From 499185b4a059b27b0a60a1bab982677c4238f062 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jayneelatintel <jayneel.vora@intel.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 13:20:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] dist-tp: tensor parallelism over RDMA at 2 and 3 ranks

- common/dist-comm.cpp: allow NetworkDirect at any world_size >= 2. Each
  ring edge negotiates ND on its own (separate send and receive
  endpoints), and only an edge without a working ND path stays on TCP.
- LLAMA_DIST_TP_RING_NEXT_HOST: the address a rank dials for its outbound
  ring edge, so the edge can use a dedicated point-to-point link instead
  of the address seen at bootstrap.
- common/dist-comm-nd.{cpp,h}: per-edge NetworkDirect endpoints.
- ggml/src/ggml-backend-meta.cpp: three fixes that only matter at 3 or
  more ranks: advance the staging buffer index on every ring step, size
  the buffer array by world_size - 1 instead of the local device count,
  and stop the host-path accumulator from adding the previous rank's
  contribution twice.
